---
name: scroll-area
type: registry:ui
title: Scroll Area
description: Augments native scroll functionality for custom, cross-browser styling.
dependencies:
  - bits-ui
files:
  - path: registry/items/components/scroll-area/scroll-area.svelte
    type: registry:ui
    target: "~/components/scroll-area/scroll-area.svelte"
  - path: registry/items/components/scroll-area/scroll-area-scrollbar.svelte
    type: registry:ui
    target: "~/components/scroll-area/scroll-area-scrollbar.svelte"
  - path: registry/items/components/scroll-area/index.ts
    type: registry:ui
    target: "~/components/scroll-area/index.ts"
---

Use scroll-area for styled scrolling regions. Set `orientation` to `vertical` (default),
`horizontal`, or `both`.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import { Separator } from '~/components/separator';
	import { ScrollArea } from '~/components/scroll-area';

	const tags = Array.from({ length: 50 }).map((_, i, a) => `v1.2.0-beta.${a.length - i}`);
</script>

<ScrollArea class="h-72 w-48 rounded-md border">
	<div class="p-4">
		<h4 class="mb-4 text-sm leading-none font-medium">Tags</h4>
		{#each tags as tag (tag)}
			<div class="text-sm">
				{tag}
			</div>
			<Separator class="my-2" />
		{/each}
	</div>
</ScrollArea>
```
